# Frontend Tech Stack Practices

Use the approved first-version stack:

- React + TypeScript
- Vite
- Cytoscape.js for graph rendering
- Static JSON data
- Zod for runtime data validation
- CSS Modules plus shared CSS tokens
- Vitest for unit tests
- Playwright for end-to-end smoke tests

Avoid adding these unless the user explicitly asks or the architecture document has been updated with the reason:

- Next.js
- Three.js
- WebSocket
- Backend services
- Databases
- Redux
- Heavy animation libraries

Prefer the simplest stable solution:

- Static data before APIs.
- CSS/Web Animations before animation libraries.
- React Context and custom hooks before state-store libraries.
- Cytoscape.js built-in graph behavior before custom graph engines.

